Silicon carbide fibres are advanced inorganic materials known for their high thermal stability, mechanical strength, chemical resistance, and low density. These characteristics make them suitable for applications in extreme operating environments where conventional materials may not deliver the required performance.

Demand is increasing as aerospace manufacturers seek materials capable of withstanding high temperatures while reducing component weight. Defense programs, advanced nuclear technologies, and industrial heating applications also create opportunities for SiC fibre suppliers. Developments in manufacturing processes and composite engineering are expected to support broader use across high-performance industries.

